{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nSplit out of the code-grounding T2 epic (`850f-bf87-8600-4af6`, ADR 0030). Terraform is **not** a\ncode-build environment — it declares cloud infrastructure and provides no language server or dependency\nresolution — so it is out of scope as a \"build env for code resolution.\" But IaC findings have their\n**own** tiered grounding that mirrors the T0/T1/T2 model in a different domain. The general lesson from\nADR 0030 is that the tiering **recurs per domain**; IaC is a distinct grounding **lane**, captured here\nas its own epic rather than folded into `850f`.\n\n## Context — the IaC tiering (to be designed)\n\n- **IaC T0 — Registry existence.** Terraform Registry provider/module existence probe (the analogue of\n  the code T0 deps-existence lane): a declared provider/module that does not exist in the Registry is a\n  refutable reference.\n- **IaC T1 — offline reference resolution.** `terraform validate` (no cloud creds, no network to a\n  provider API): validates that references between resources/variables/outputs resolve within the\n  configuration. Offline + deterministic-ish → the IaC analogue of the T1 syntactic floor.\n- **IaC T2 — live plan.** `terraform plan` (needs cloud credentials + provider API access): the\n  high-fidelity, non-deterministic, credential-bearing tier — the analogue of code T2, and subject to\n  the same confirm-only + never-on-a-blocking-path constraints (plus a credential-handling/security\n  design, since `plan` authenticates to a cloud account).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Decide the v1 IaC tier(s) to implement among Registry existence (T0), `terraform validate` (T1),\n      and `terraform plan` (T2), with the determinism/credential/security tradeoffs recorded in an ADR.\n- [ ] The chosen tier(s) emit the existing three-valued evidence contract at the correct provenance\n      tier, with no change to the contract or its consumers.\n- [ ] IaC resolution is self-contained + opt-in (gated behind config / an optional extra) and\n      fail-open (missing `terraform` binary / no creds / timeout → `abstain` with a closed reason).\n- [ ] `terraform plan` (if in v1 scope) never runs on a deterministic blocking path and never carries\n      credentials into an untrusted context; otherwise it is explicitly deferred with rationale.\n- [ ] Fail-open matrix tested per implemented tier.\n- [ ] An IaC grounding lane exists that emits the same three-valued, fail-open evidence contract\n- [ ] IaC resolution is confirm-only and off any deterministic blocking path unless a tier is proven"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785007207873808001,"uuid":"d5827511-0080-44aa-8855-aa296011f706"}